This program exists to prove that sysmon's mutator slot is bracketed `blocked`
(#4734, from #4287's triage). Since #4060 the slot is claimed unconditionally at
`threadTrampoline`, and `sysmonRun` is `@nosplit` end to end, so it can never
acknowledge an epoch: without its one `gcBlockingBegin()` line every rendezvous
burns `stwSpinBound` and gives up. Abandoning is SAFE — nothing is corrupted and
no output changes — so the abandoned count is the only oracle. The program is
built so an unbracketed entry body is the sole possible cause: it starts no
thread of its own, and the only threads alive are the ones boot starts, whose
bodies are either bracketed around their park or reach safepoints.
